      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Looking at DefaultDOManager.java in trunk (post-3.4), the doRegistry table is updated without escaping DB-specific escape characters (apostrophes are handled, however).  Updates to this table should be made using a PreparedStatement instead, so the JDBC driver can do the right thing.  Note: the only other table that contains varchar or text data is doFields, and that was updated some time ago to use PreparedStatements for a similar reason.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
